From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sargun Vohra <sargunv@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 04:16:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Carry plugin static textures

Lets a plugin shader declare up to three static RGBA32F data textures that
its fragment stage reads by exact texel. Registration validates and copies
the bytes; each renderer uploads them once, on first use, and shares them
among every style layer of the type, and a failed upload makes the shader
draw nothing instead of sampling another texture. Includes registry and
rendering tests on OpenGL, Metal and Vulkan, among them a layer uniform
block read by both shader stages. Not yet proposed upstream.

Carried by maplibre-plugins until it lands upstream.
