+`0028-plugin-static-textures.patch` adds static data textures to plugin
+shaders. A shader descriptor lists up to three RGBA32F textures of at most
+2048 texels a side; registration validates and copies their bytes, and
+re-registering different bytes conflicts. Each renderer uploads a texture once,
+on first use, with nearest filtering and clamp-to-edge addressing, and every
+style layer of the type shares it; a failed upload is logged once and the
+shader draws nothing. Shaders read the texture from the fragment stage through
+`MLN_PLUGIN_TEXTURE_<id>_BINDING`, and OpenGL resolves the sampler by name. The
+patch includes registry validation tests, which check that each rejection comes
+from the check it targets, and rendering tests on every backend: exact texel
+reads in row order, one upload shared across layers, drawable rebuilds and new
+tiles, a later renderer uploading again, sampler resolution in both shader
+variants, a source-free layer, and a layer uniform block read by both shader
+stages. This patch is not yet proposed upstream.
+
 Each patch is the squashed diff of its upstream branch, applied on top of the
 patches before it, so a patch that adds a test next to an earlier patch's test
 carries that placement rather than the branch's own context.
